	(text "Same relays and terminal as the MES2_Extension \"WINCH CONTROL\": TE IM03GR, 5 V coil (178 Ω, 28 mA) from\n+5V_24, contacts 2 A / 220 VDC, 60 W DC. They only switch the 48 V winch controller's direction inputs to\nJ18 pin 2 (COM): pin 1 = CLK, pin 3 = ACLK. They are not rated for the winch motor current.\nTE terminal assignment: coil 1 (+) / 8 (-); pole 1: 3 COM, 2 NC, 4 NO; pole 2: 6 COM, 7 NC, 5 NO.\n\nDrivers as on the relay sheets (CIF §7a): AO3400A, 100 Ω gate, 100k pull-down, so both relays are OFF\nduring reset and boot (the gate inputs float then). The Extension used 2SC2884 transistors without a pull-down.\n\nHardware interlock (new, uses the spare second pole): CLK closes COM → ILK_CLK → K5 NO1 → CLK only\nwhile K6 rests (its NC2 feeds ILK_CLK), and the same the other way. If both relays are energised, both\noutputs stay open, so the winch can never see both directions at once. Firmware still drives only one.\n\nTODO (HANDOFF.md step 2): the gate resistors are not driven yet. PA0 / PA1 went back to relay coil feedback\n(MES4 standard); the winch moves to TCA9535 outputs + KAQY214S photoMOS relays."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 156.21 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "85ae40bb-cdd4-5b38-b2f0-bab5c419ca98")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 201.93 20.32)
		(end 403.86 147.32)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "b31d7f02-8a32-5a1c-810f-1c2df2b0b19b")
	)
